course: dictionary
lesson: 5808
title: Real magic or clever tricks?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A magician is a performer who does tricks that seem impossible, like making things disappear. Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «A magician in Dublin made a girl's watch vanish from a box and appear in his pocket» tells you the magician does something clever with a box and a pocket.
explain: Stories and real life use the word in different ways. In a tale, a magician can have real magic powers, like a wizard. «The Magician makes a deal» shows a magician who can really cast magic. In real life, a stage magician uses secret skills, fast hands and distraction instead.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «A party magician» still makes sense if you think of a performer who does tricks at a party, so you have the right idea.
fact: A magician is a performer who does tricks that seem impossible.
fact: In stories, a magician has real magic powers, like a wizard.
fact: In real life, stage magicians use secret skills, fast hands and distraction, not real magic.
fact: «Magicians traditionally keep their secrets, so keeping your trick's secret is fine and not a lie.»
fact: Other phrases to know: «a party magician» and «the magician's assistant».
exercise: «A magician in Dublin made a girl's watch vanish from a box.» What is a magician? | *Someone who does tricks that seem impossible | A teacher who runs a school | A girl who loses her watch | A type of bird that lives by the sea
exercise: In real life, how do stage magicians make their tricks work? | By calling a wizard for help | With real magic powers | By asking the audience to wish hard | *With secret skills, fast hands and distraction
exercise: What does «a party magician» mean? | A dancer who wears a big hat | A cook who makes food for parties | *A performer who does tricks at parties | A person who is always late to parties
test: «Magicians traditionally keep their secrets.» Why is keeping a trick's secret fine? | Because the audience asked for it | Because secrets are always lies | *Because it is not a lie, it is part of the show | Because tricks are real magic
test: In the folk tale, what does the Magician do? | *Makes a deal with Pau Amma | Sings songs at a party | Builds a castle on the hill | Sells his magic hat
exam: Which is the best meaning of magician in real life? | A king who rules a faraway land | *A performer who does tricks that seem impossible | A baker who makes bread every morning | A sailor who stirs up the sea
